NEARS-3640 QA — live-reproduced task_bug (HIGH, breaks_ac: EP2)
Device: emulator-5556, package com.izzes.nears.nears_nears_3640_edit_profile_redesign

Repro:
1. Edit Profile screen, dirty a field (email changed to a different value), tap Update while
   offline (or any path where profileServiceInterface.updateProfile(...) throws — see the sibling
   bug-save-success-popscope-reentrancy.log / the pre-existing ProfileRepository NoSuchMethodError
   for one concrete trigger).
2. The awaited call inside `ProfileController.updateUserInfo()` throws before returning.
3. `_isLoading = false; update();` at the tail of `updateUserInfo()` is NEVER REACHED (no
   try/catch/finally wraps the awaited call) -- `_isLoading` stays `true` forever.
4. Confirmed via uiautomator: `content-desc="Update, loading" clickable=false enabled=false`
   persists even after:
     - discarding the dirty field back to its original (clean) value,
     - fully navigating away (Back -> Profile) and back into a freshly-rebuilt Edit Profile screen.
   Only a full app restart (force-stop + relaunch) resets it, because `ProfileController` is a
   permanent `GetxService` (`Get.put`, never disposed) whose `_isLoading` field survives screen
   remounts.

Source (profile_controller.dart:131-161, unchanged in this respect by the fix-cycle):
  Future<ResponseModel> updateUserInfo(...) async {
    updateUserModel.imageDeleted = _imageMarkedForRemoval;
    if (fromButton) { _isLoading = true; update(); }
    ResponseModel responseModel = await profileServiceInterface.updateProfile(updateUserModel, _pickedFile, token);
    if (!fromVerification) { _updateProfileResponseHandle(...); }
    _isLoading = false;   // unreachable if the awaited call above throws
    update();
    return responseModel;
  }

NButton's onPressed gate (update_profile_screen.dart:603) is NEW code from this ticket:
  onPressed: (profileController.isLoading || !dirty) ? null : ...

Effect: ANY exception thrown while `profileServiceInterface.updateProfile(...)` is in flight --
not limited to the specific pre-existing null-body NoSuchMethodError this QA pass happened to
trigger -- permanently disables Save for the REST OF THE APP SESSION. The user has no way to
recover except force-killing and reopening the app; there is no visible error message explaining
why Save stopped working, and it silently affects every future visit to Edit Profile, not just the
one where the failure happened.

Root cause is a missing try/finally around the isLoading toggle in a NEW call site this ticket's
own EP2 dirty-gate directly depends on -- matches the active review-lesson
`isloading-flag-omitted-try-catch-sibling-methods` this session's lessons-read selector surfaced
for this exact ticket before build. breaks_ac: true (EP2 -- Save must recover to a usable state
after a failed attempt, not permanently disable itself).
